node_modules/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store

# per-project outcome records and tuning (raw data, never committed)
.ursa/

# Trial outputs: real outcome records and their viewers, built from real
# sessions. Never committed, and until now nothing said so — the docs cite
# ursa-major/trial/task-001/ and no branch has ever carried it. The
# redaction gate is a backstop, not this one's: it looks for session UUIDs,
# home paths and project slugs, and a record built from pasted
# conversations (fixtures/mini uses ids like 01-claude) carries verbatim
# prompt text with none of those shapes.
ursa-major/trial/*/

# Run scratch, inside the working tree on purpose.
#
# Seat runs on the resident host share /tmp: it is mode 1777, TMPDIR is
# unset, and every seat runs as the same user, so a bare /tmp/<noun> name is
# a shared mutable path and not a private one. On 2026-10-26 HQ's
# distribution seat composed a pull request body at such a path, a sibling
# seat wrote the same filename in between, and `gh pr edit` published the
# sibling's body. Both writes succeeded and no exit status reported it.
#
# The real repair is a private scratch directory exported by whatever
# provisions a run, and it is filed as a ledger entry. Until that exists, a
# run has two safe options: `mktemp -d`, or a path under this directory.
# This entry is what makes the second one safe, because the in-tree
# workaround is otherwise one `git add -A` away from committing a pull
# request body, and the seats that have used it so far relied on
# remembering to delete the file by hand.
.scratch/
#
# The same idea spelled differently, because the rule above is one exact
# directory name and a run that has to remember a name does not remember
# that one. On 2026-10-26 an exo window shipped a ship-first placeholder
# at `.exo-window-52-scratch` in the repository root, 75 bytes of benign
# text, and it is in `main`'s history permanently. Nothing was disclosed
# and that is luck, not a control: the hazard this rule exists to blunt is
# that the in-tree workaround is one `git add -A` away from committing
# whatever the run happened to be composing. No tracked file in this
# repository has ever had `scratch` in its name, so these cost nothing.
*-scratch
*.scratch
.scratch-*
scratch/
